# NEXUS Research Methods Standard

Every doctoral programme must select methods appropriate to its claims.

## Permitted methodological families

1. Design-science research
2. Controlled experiments
3. Ablation studies
4. Simulation
5. Benchmark comparison
6. Longitudinal observation
7. Case study
8. Mixed methods
9. Qualitative analysis
10. Independent replication

## Required controls

Every study must define:

- research question;
- falsifiable hypothesis;
- null hypothesis;
- independent variables;
- dependent variables;
- control condition;
- baseline;
- dataset;
- inclusion criteria;
- exclusion criteria;
- metrics;
- statistical analysis;
- failure criteria;
- ethical risks;
- reproducibility package;
- limitations.

## Prohibited practices

- changing primary metrics after observing results without disclosure;
- excluding failed runs without a recorded rule;
- selecting only favourable datasets;
- treating repository implementation as scientific validation;
- claiming causation from observational evidence alone;
- reporting performance without uncertainty;
- hiding negative or null findings.

