# Ablation Standard

Each claimed NEXUS contribution should be isolated where possible.

Candidate ablations:

- no governance layer;
- no persistent memory;
- no evidence graph;
- no specialist agents;
- single-agent baseline;
- no data-truth gate;
- no human approval;
- no local-first continuity;
- no knowledge graph;
- no commissioning gate.

Ablation results must include uncertainty and failure analysis.

