# NEXUS Research Position

NEXUS is investigated as a governed, local-first, multi-agent cognitive and
engineering operating system supporting heterogeneous domain systems.

## Primary comparative position

NEXUS combines:

- cognitive architectures;
- persistent memory;
- multi-agent orchestration;
- software-engineering agents;
- evidence and provenance;
- executable governance;
- human approval;
- commissioning;
- local/cloud distribution;
- domain-specific intelligence.

## Main claimed distinction requiring empirical validation

Existing research commonly studies these capabilities separately.

NEXUS proposes that they can operate under one traceable authority, evidence,
memory and engineering model.

This is a research proposition, not an established result.

