# Research Provenance Policy

Every paper, dataset, claim, experiment and synthesis must record:

1. original source;
2. author or producing institution;
3. acquisition date;
4. canonical identifier;
5. licence;
6. content hash where locally stored;
7. transformation history;
8. reviewer;
9. verification date;
10. lifecycle status.

Generated summaries must never replace the source record.

